{"document.score": 0.40952203470000004, "document.content": "Ball, a Singapore-based Asia editor of the journal, had told Cheng she would speak to her own supervisor, who would then speak to executive-level staff about the matter. There was no evidence that Ball represented the “directing mind or will” of Dow Jones, Tsoi said.

The conversation between Cheng and Ball was recorded on the reporter’s phone. The audio recording and a transcript of the call were saved onto a USB stick and submitted to the court.

“It was clear as day Ball could not make the decision, hence she [had] to go back to her higher supervisor, who then would have to go back to the executive branch in New York,” he said. “This is a broken gap in the evidence that Ms Cheng cannot fill [with] hearsay evidence.”", "document.metadata": {"chunk_number": 457, "file_name": "09-03-2026_Hong Kong court rejects Wall Street Journal’s bid to throw out wrongful dismissal suit.txt", "source_folder": "hk_free_press_news", "source_type": "news_txt", "article_title": "Hong Kong court rejects Wall Street Journal’s bid to throw out wrongful dismissal suit", "file_path": "C:\Program Files\Studying\coding\RAG_project\data\hk_free_press_news\09-03-2026_Hong Kong court rejects Wall Street Journal’s bid to throw out wrongful dismissal suit.txt", "article_date": "09-03-2026", "chunk_size": 800, "chunk_overlap": 120}, "document.id": "321b3579-1526-4294-adfa-1177b24c025f"}
